        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Trionfo Beccaccino',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trionfo Beccaccino (also Marafone Beccaccino) is a 4-player partnership trick-taking game from Romagna, Italy. It combines Tressette scoring (3-2-A ranking) with a trump suit (Trionfa). The 4â™¦ holder chooses trump. The Maraffa/Cricca (A+2+3 of trumps) earns 3 bonus points. Game to 41.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Marafon-Beccaccino is characteristic of the Italian province of Romagna. It is a four-player partnership game based on Tressette with the addition of a trump suit. The first printed reference to Beccaccino appears in 1971 in Libero Ercolani\'s Vocabolario romagnolo-italiano (Ravenna). Earlier the game was known as "tri sett cun el taj" (Tressette with cutting). The composite name Marafon-Beccaccino was coined in Alteo Dolcini\'s Il Principe di Romagna (Imola, 1975), which codified official rules.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 (partnerships)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40 cards (Romagnole). Rank: 3-2-A-K-Kt-J-7-6-5-4. Values: A=1, 3/2/K/Kt/J=1/3.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '10 cards each. 4â™¦ holder chooses trump.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
